const body = `<h1>2.4a — Scanner: Let the User Talk Back</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity discovery">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Discovery Lab</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Explore: Hello Scanner</h3>
        <p>So far your programs talk AT the user. Today you'll let the user talk BACK. Java's Scanner class reads what the user types.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>ScannerExplore</code>. Type this code exactly:</p>
        <div class="code-block"><pre>import java.util.Scanner;

public class ScannerExplore {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("What is your name? ");
        String name = input.nextLine();

        System.out.print("How old are you? ");
        int age = input.nextInt();

        System.out.println("Hello, " + name + "! You are " + age + " years old.");
        input.close();
    }
}</pre></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Experiment</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Run it. Type your name and age. Does it work?</li>
            <li>Now type your full name (like "Ada Lovelace"). What happens to age? Why?</li>
            <li>After the <code>nextInt()</code> call, add a second <code>input.nextLine()</code> — what does that line do? Why is it needed?</li>
            <li>Try <code>nextDouble()</code> instead of <code>nextInt()</code>. What happens if you type "twelve" instead of 12?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Document</h3>
        <p>Answer in your lab notes:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>What does <code>new Scanner(System.in)</code> do?</li>
            <li>What's the difference between <code>nextLine()</code> and <code>nextInt()</code>?</li>
            <li>What's the "leftover newline" problem and how do you fix it?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/scanner.html">Scanner Input</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/printing.html">Printing &amp; Output</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
